WEBVTT

00:00:00.174 --> 00:00:04.724
One thin strip of land, about 20
kilometres wide, holds India together.

00:00:04.769 --> 00:00:07.739
The Siliguri Corridor,
the "Chicken's Neck",

00:00:07.749 --> 00:00:09.819
links the northeast to the rest of India.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.080
Nepal, Bhutan and Bangladesh sit
on its sides, and China is not far.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.551
Rail, roads, pipelines and
power lines all pass through it.

00:00:17.551 --> 00:00:21.201
If it were blocked, the northeast's
supplies would need much longer routes.

00:00:21.401 --> 00:00:23.491
That is why India has built up roads,

00:00:24.101 --> 00:00:26.031
rail links and forces around the corridor,

00:00:26.321 --> 00:00:28.551
and is working on other
routes through the region.

00:00:28.602 --> 00:00:31.891
It's one of the most watched few
kilometres on any map of Asia.

00:00:32.002 --> 00:00:33.692
Should India build a second route?

00:00:33.707 --> 00:00:34.337
Comment.

